          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.12,
            0.651,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which of the following could be the other number:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.149,
            0.286,
            0.17
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2, 3, 5, 8, 10?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.188,
            0.274,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Jump Jackpot"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.217,
            0.466,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Jumpy and Grumpy play a game."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.241,
            0.833,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grumpy places a treasure on some number. For example, he may place it on 24."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.286,
            0.833,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Jumpy chooses a jump size. If he chooses 4, then he has to jump only on multiples of 4, starting at 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.332,
            0.834,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Jumpy gets the treasure if he lands on the number where Grumpy placed it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.381,
            0.832,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Which jump sizes will get Jumpy to land on 24? If he chooses 4: Jumpy lands on 4 → 8 → 12 → 16 → 20 → 24 → 28 → ... Other successful jump sizes are 2, 3, 6, 8 and 12."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.453,
            0.827,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.125,
                0.453,
                0.827,
                0.606
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.619,
            0.833,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What about the jump of sizes 1 and 24? Yes, they also will land on 24."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.665,
            0.833,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24 all divide 24 exactly. Recall that such numbers are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "factors",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "divisors",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of 24."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.711,
            0.835,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grumpy increases the level of the game. Two treasures are kept on two different numbers. Jumpy has to choose a jump size and stick to it. Jumpy gets the treasures only if he lands on both the numbers with the chosen jump size. As before, Jumpy starts at 0."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.802,
            0.833,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grumpy has kept the treasures on 14 and 36. And, Jumpy chooses a jump size of 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.847,
            0.835,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Will Jumpy land on both the treasures? Starting from 0, he jumps to 7 → 14 → 21 → 28 → 35 → 42 … We see that he landed on 14 but"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 17,
